# PART X — PERFORMANCE AND ACCOUNTABILITY INDICATORS

## 12. Proposed Measurement Architecture

The framework should avoid relying on a single institutional integrity score.

Instead, it should use a multidimensional performance register.

|Indicator|Measurement objective|
|---|---|
|Source Completeness|Proportion of required records accounted for.|
|Provenance Reliability|Percentage of records with documented origin and custody.|
|Statutory Traceability|Proportion of findings mapped to applicable legal provisions.|
|Authority Verification|Percentage of examined decisions with identified authority.|
|Financial Traceability|Proportion of assessed expenditures supported by auditable records.|
|Procurement Integrity|Compliance with applicable procurement requirements.|
|Ecological Performance|Measured environmental outcomes against defined baselines.|
|Corrective Completion|Verified completion of assigned remediation actions.|
|Participation Coverage|Representation of relevant stakeholders and affected communities.|
|Temporal Resilience|Continuity of accountability and performance over time.|

### Rating Rules

Every rating must disclose:

- Measurement formula.
- Data source.
- Reporting period.
- Evaluation threshold.
- Confidence level.
- Missing information.
- Independent verification status.

No rating should imply certainty beyond the quality of its supporting evidence.

